Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied file contains diagnosis code only; the NextItNet backbone and 
representation readout are not shown. The probe accesses item embeddings through
`view.item_emb`, item count through `view.model.itemnum`, sequence features 
through `view.log2feats(sequence)`, and logits through 
`view.predict_score(features, items)`. It scores every valid training position, 
so it does not verify that final-user inference correctly reads the final 
nonpadding position in left-padded histories.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view, metadata, review 
data, and training histories. Reviews and histories are not directly used by 
these probes. `run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` samples item embeddings and 
examines up to ten batches containing `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
tensors of shape B × L.

For each batch, it switches the view to evaluation mode, computes sequence 
features, stacks positive and negative item IDs, and requests paired logits. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Computation uses no gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings with seed 42,
excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 corresponds to mean cosine 
similarity zero.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive logit minus 
sampled-negative logit. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins indicate 
stronger separation. Lower negative-wins and small-margin rates are preferable; 
the latter uses margin < 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive- and negative-item categories 
separately for low-margin and wrong-rank positions, retaining the top twenty. 
These are raw counts, not normalized category error rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequences are shuffled, masked, reordered, or otherwise perturbed. Sampled 
negatives test local ranking separation, not sensitivity to history changes.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` with six entries: `embedding_collapse_score`, 
four `pos_neg_*` separation metrics, and `pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`; 
`metric_definitions` explains each. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both 
dictionaries and requests JSON containing `status`, `core_findings`, 
`key_implications`, and `evidence`.

Item categories are unavailable under this task’s data contract, so category 
lists should remain empty. These training-sample probes do not measure 
validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal sensitivity, or simulator 
traits. Empty margin samples return zeros, which can misleadingly resemble 
healthy error rates.

