Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied file contains diagnosis code only; the NextItNet backbone and final
inference readout are not shown. Diagnosis accesses item embeddings through 
`view.item_emb.weight` and obtains position-level sequence representations 
through `view.log2feats(sequence)`. It does not explicitly select a final user 
representation or verify that inference reads the final nonpadding position of 
left-padded histories.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view, its metadata, 
review data, and training histories. Only metadata is subsequently used 
directly. `view.model` provides the actual model and item count; the view 
exposes evaluation mode, embeddings, feature extraction, and scoring.

The training loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors
shaped B × L. For up to ten batches, sequences become NumPy inputs to 
`log2feats`; positive and negative IDs are stacked into B × L × 2 candidates. 
`predict_score(features, items)` returns their logits. Positions with positive 
ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Sample up to 2,048 real-item embeddings with seed 42, 
excluding padding and reserved tokens. Normalize embeddings, average 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and map the result to [0,1]. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately orthogonal embeddings score around 
0.5.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Compute positive minus negative logits at 
valid positions. Report the mean, tenth percentile, fraction below zero, and 
fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower failure fractions generally 
indicate stronger sampled training separation.
- **Category breakdown:** Count category occurrences separately for positive and
negative items in weak-margin and wrong-ranking positions, reporting the top 
twenty categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, masking, or sensitivity test is performed. 
Random embedding subsampling estimates geometry; supplied negatives test 
pairwise ranking. Scoring runs in evaluation mode without gradients.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering the 
six outputs above. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into instructions 
requesting JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`; it does not itself generate that interpretation.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog recommendation 
quality, temporal sensitivity, gradients, or simulator traits. Category metadata
is unavailable in this task, so category lists should be empty. Missing valid 
samples produce zero margin statistics, which can misleadingly appear healthy.

