Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains only the diagnosis module; the NextItNet backbone and
final sequence readout implementation are not shown. Diagnosis accesses item 
embeddings through `view.item_emb.weight`, per-position sequence representations
through `view.log2feats(sequence)`, and candidate logits through 
`view.predict_score(features, items)`. It evaluates all valid training 
positions, rather than explicitly selecting a final user representation. Correct
final-position readout for left-padded histories cannot be verified here.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view (named `model` in 
the constructor), including `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. The 
underlying network is `view.model`; its `itemnum` bounds the real-item embedding
slice. Reviews and stored histories are not otherwise used by these probes.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with B × L tensors. 
Sequences become NumPy arrays before feature extraction. Positive and negative 
IDs are stacked into B × L × 2 candidates for scoring; positions with positive 
ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples at most 2,048 real-item embeddings using seed 
42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the 
result to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger directional alignment; 
approximately 0.5 means mean cosine near zero.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Uses up to ten loader batches in evaluation 
mode without gradients. Computes positive minus negative logits at valid 
positions. Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins indicate stronger 
separation. Lower negative-beats-positive and small-margin rates are preferable;
the latter uses margin < 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive/negative item category occurrences for
low-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, reporting the top 20 categories 
separately. These are raw counts, without exposure normalization. Categories are
unavailable under the stated task, so these lists should be empty.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, ablation, or sensitivity test runs. Random 
embedding subsampling estimates geometric alignment; sampled negative 
comparisons measure training-position discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`, 
containing the six metrics above. Missing valid margins produce zeros, which can
misleadingly appear healthy.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries into a prompt requesting
JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does
not generate that interpretation itself.

The diagnosis does not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal 
sensitivity, representation rank, gradients, or unobserved simulator traits. 
Margin thresholds also depend on logit scale.

