Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The task specifies a NextItNet backbone, but its implementation is not included.
Diagnosis accesses a model adapter through `item_emb`, `log2feats(sequence)` and
`predict_score(features, items)`; the underlying network is `view.model`.

`log2feats` supplies sequence features for scoring every training position. The 
probe does not explicitly select a final user representation. Final-position 
readout and correct handling of left padding cannot be verified from this file.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the adapter and its `meta_data`, 
`review_data` and `user_train` attributes. Reviews and user histories are not 
subsequently used.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped `B 
× L`. For up to ten batches, the probe computes sequence features, stacks 
positive/negative IDs into `B × L × 2`, and obtains paired logits. Positions 
with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings using seed
42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It averages pairwise cosine 
similarities and maps the result to `[0,1]`. Higher values indicate directional 
alignment; roughly 0.5 corresponds to zero mean cosine similarity.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower-tail 
positive-minus-negative logits. Higher values indicate stronger sampled-pair 
separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction of negative margins; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction of margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts category labels among 
low-margin and incorrectly ranked positive/negative items, retaining the top 
twenty labels per group.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, shuffle tests, or sensitivity experiments. 
Embedding subsampling estimates geometry; positive/negative comparisons assess 
training-pair discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into instructions requesting JSON 
with `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does not 
itself generate that interpretation.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, generalization, full-catalog 
ranking, or sequence-order sensitivity. Margin magnitudes depend on logit scale.
Missing valid positions produce potentially misleading zero summaries. Item 
categories are unavailable in this benchmark, so category lists should be empty.
Mean cosine similarity alone cannot establish representation quality or rule out
other forms of collapse.

