Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses a sequential model through a compatibility view; the
NextItNet backbone itself is not shown. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)`. The margin probe 
uses features at every valid training position, rather than extracting a final 
user representation. Final inference readout cannot be verified here; 
left-padded histories require the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view and its `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently consulted; 
reviews and histories are not directly analyzed.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors of shape `B ×
L`. For up to ten batches, sequences pass through `log2feats`; positive and 
negative IDs are stacked into `B × L × 2` candidates and scored with 
`predict_score`. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Margin 
computation uses evaluation mode and disables gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings with seed 42, 
excluding padding and reserved tokens. It averages off-diagonal cosine 
similarities and maps the result to `[0,1]`. Higher values indicate directional 
similarity; approximately 0.5 means mean cosine near zero, not necessarily 
collapse.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive logit minus 
sampled-negative logit. Reports mean, tenth percentile, negative-wins rate, and 
fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower failure rates generally indicate 
stronger separation.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item categories 
separately for weak-margin and wrong-rank positions, retaining the top twenty 
categories. Counts are not normalized for exposure.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, ablation, or order-sensitivity test occurs.
Randomness only subsamples embeddings; negatives come from the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering the 
six entries above. The breakdown includes thresholds, position totals, and 
category counts. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and 
requests JSON containing `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, gradients, 
temporal sensitivity, or simulator traits. Categories are unavailable in this 
task, so category lists remain empty. Empty valid batches yield zero margin 
statistics, which must not be interpreted as measured health.

