Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe observes the NextItNet model through its compatibility view. Relevant 
hooks are `item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features,
items)`; `view.model` is the actual trained module. Backbone implementation and 
final sequence readout are not shown. Diagnosis scores features at each valid 
training position, so it does not verify that inference correctly reads the 
final nonpadding position of left-padded histories.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the view, device, metadata, review data, 
and training histories. Only metadata is subsequently queried; review data and 
histories are unused.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` tensors shaped B × L.
For up to ten batches, sequences pass through `log2feats`; positive and negative
IDs are stacked into B × L × 2 candidates and scored through `predict_score`. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Scoring runs in evaluation mode 
without gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings with seed 42, 
excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes embeddings, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. Higher indicates
stronger directional alignment; approximately 0.5 represents zero average cosine
similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive minus negative logits. 
Higher mean and tenth-percentile margins suggest stronger separation. Lower 
negative-wins and small-margin rates are preferable; the small-margin threshold 
is 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item categories 
separately for low-margin and wrong-ranking positions, retaining the top twenty 
categories. These are raw counts, without exposure normalization. Categories are
unavailable in this task, so these lists should be empty.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffle, ablation, or sensitivity test runs. Random 
embedding subsampling and loader-provided negatives are the only sampling 
mechanisms.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics contain
`embedding_collapse_score`, `pos_neg_margin_mean`, `pos_neg_margin_p10`, 
`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`, `pos_neg_small_margin_rate`, and 
`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and requests a JSON 
interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence. It does not 
itself generate that interpretation.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog quality, gradients, 
causal sensitivity, or inference/checkpoint consistency. Margins depend on score
scale and negative sampling; empty margin observations produce zeros that can 
appear healthy.

