Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['Deletion changes 
history length, receptive-field membership, and target distance simultaneously. 
The protocol needs matched controls before attributing margin changes to 
stale-history interference.', 'The implementation is not fully reproducible: 
deletion fractions, recent-window sizes, permutation counts, random seeds, 
aggregation weights, tolerances, and diagnostic runtime limits are unspecified. 
Training-position averages also overweight longer histories.', 'Mean embedding 
cosine measures directional alignment rather than collapse. Raw score margins 
depend on embedding and logit scale, so neither measurement alone establishes 
useful discrimination. The difficulty rating of 3 appears optimistic given 
architecture inspection and padding controls.'], generating follow-up queries
