Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['Padding-ID ablation may
introduce artifacts: convolution biases and normalization can produce nonzero 
hidden states at masked positions. Bands that include the final item also 
conflict with final-nonpadding readout. Define whether lag zero is excluded, 
retain the original readout anchor, and handle histories emptied by masking.', 
'Receptive-field accounting must include residual branches and any normalization
or pooling that mixes temporal positions. The report lacks exact lag bands, 
eligible-history rules, aggregation weights, uncertainty estimates, runtime 
limits, and a reproducible sampling procedure.', 'One positive and one negative 
support paired margins and ranking flips, not meaningful HR@10 or top-10 
overlap. Those metrics require an explicitly available larger candidate set. 
Training-loader sensitivity also cannot establish generalization or harmful 
reliance on older events.', 'The originality rating is reasonable, but future 
potential remains speculative and difficulty may be understated until padding 
behavior and predictor consistency are verified. Zero-ID masking should be 
compared with controlled replacements before its effects motivate recency 
regularization.'], generating follow-up queries
