Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis inspects the trained NextItNet through ModelView. Relevant components 
are item embeddings, residual causal convolution blocks, optional gated 
recent-history summaries, normalization and positional embeddings. 
`log2feats(sequence)` produces position-wise features; the sequence 
representation uses the maximum nonpadding index in a left-padded history. 
Backbone implementation details are accessed through hooks rather than supplied 
here.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains `view.model`, embeddings, training 
histories and metadata interfaces. It calls `log2feats` and 
`predict_score(features, items)` for features and scores. The loader supplies 
`(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with aligned B × L tensors. Diagnosis 
runs without gradients in evaluation mode, seeds randomness to 42, and restores 
module modes and random states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding cosine:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings and maps mean 
pairwise cosine to [0,1]. Higher values indicate greater alignment; 0.5 means 
zero mean cosine. Alignment alone cannot establish collapse or quality.
- **Training margins:** Across ten batches, measures positive-minus-negative 
score mean, tenth percentile, negative-margin rate and margin-below-0.5 rate. 
Larger margins and fewer negative margins indicate stronger sampled training 
separation.
- **Training-prefix ranking:** Samples up to twelve users and two prefixes each.
Computes exact eligible-catalog ranks and user-averaged HR@10, excluding 
previously observed items except the target. Lower ranks and higher HR indicate 
better in-sample fit.
- **Architecture checks:** Reports structural receptive offsets, future-token 
leakage, all-padding feature norms and position-shift sensitivity. Near-zero 
causality error is expected; structural reachability does not measure 
importance.

# Perturbation & Tests

Tests compare original histories with frequency-matched recent/older deletions, 
frequency-and-lag-matched deletion controls, full permutations and 
terminal-preserving permutations. Candidates and sampled negatives remain fixed.
Outputs include rank, HR@10 and margin changes, top-ten overlap, 
control-adjusted effects and recent-minus-older contrasts. Deletion-induced 
position shifts and reachability changes are recorded. User-bootstrap intervals 
quantify sampled-user uncertainty. Replacement probes are disabled; a synthetic 
check validates ranking ties and chunking.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
protocol, coverage, architecture, margins, baseline/paired observations, 
intervention aggregates, strata and cost. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` 
requests a grounded JSON interpretation.

These probes measure training fit and sensitivity, not held-out generalization. 
Matching failures and sparse samples limit conclusions. Unavailable metadata, 
replacement effects and four-category macro estimates remain empty or null. 
Pinned host macro validation HR@10 governs selection.

