Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe targets the supplied NextItNet causal residual convolution backbone. 
It inspects `item_emb` and residual blocks’ `conv1`/`conv2` kernels and 
dilations. `log2feats(sequence)` produces per-position representations; final 
scoring selects the largest nonzero sequence index, correctly handling left 
padding. `predict_score(features, items)` scores positive/negative targets.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual module through `view.model`, 
plus embeddings, histories and metadata through ModelView. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` snapshots at most four batches and 32 rows 
per batch, each containing `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching 
B × L tensors.

Diagnosis runs without gradients in evaluation mode, seeds its random draws, and
restores module modes, RNG states and temporary hooks. An embedding forward hook
selectively zeros input embeddings; it is removed before target scoring.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 catalog embeddings, excluding 
padding, and maps mean pairwise cosine to `(cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values 
indicate stronger alignment; 0.5 means mean cosine zero, not a collapse 
probability.
- **Target separation:** Reports mean and tenth-percentile 
positive-minus-negative margins, negative-win frequency and margins below 0.5, 
across supported positions and separately at final positions. Larger margins and
fewer negative wins indicate stronger sampled-pair separation; margins depend on
score scale.
- **Implementation checks:** Tests future invariance, aligned-prefix equivalence
and ModelView versus actual-module candidate scores. Finite, close results 
support consistency on sampled inputs.
- **Dependency checks:** Propagates convolution offsets through residual 
branches and measures final-feature responses to selected input replacements. 
Unexpected effects at unreachable offsets suggest topology or implementation 
problems.

# Perturbation & Tests

Recent and older interventions remove equal-sized, disjoint history subsets 
while retaining the final event. Each compares survivor repacking with 
fixed-position embedding ablation. Five prefix-shuffle draws preserve the final 
event, padding and item multiset. Paired outputs report score, margin and 
negative-win-rate changes on unchanged targets. Sensitivity establishes neither 
accuracy nor causal temporal importance.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering probe 
summaries, support/exclusion counts, perturbations, structure, checks and 
configuration. Undefined measurements are null. Category evidence, deployment 
reload parity and validation ranking metrics are explicitly unavailable. Bounded
rows may repeat users; no user-level confidence intervals or benchmark HR@10 are
inferred. The interpreter requests grounded JSON findings with status, 
implications and evidence.

