Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis inspects the trained NextItNet through a ModelView. Relevant 
components are item embeddings, causal sequence features, candidate scoring, and
gated convolution blocks. `log2feats(sequence)` produces positionwise 
representations; diagnostic histories are truncated, left-padded, and read at 
the maximum nonpadding index. Structural analysis recognizes specific gated 
NextItNet source patterns; the model implementation itself is not supplied here.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses `view.model`, `item_emb`, `log2feats`, 
`predict_score`, and training histories. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` as aligned B × L tensors. Probes run without gradients in 
evaluation mode, restoring module modes and Python/NumPy/PyTorch RNG states 
afterward.

Training-only prefix sampling uses seed 42, up to 12 users and two cuts per 
user. Catalog scoring excludes previously seen full-prefix items except the 
target, with deterministic ascending-ID tie breaks.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** sampled mean pairwise cosine mapped to [0,1]; 
approximately 0.5 indicates zero mean cosine. This alone cannot establish 
collapse or quality.
- **Training margins:** mean, lower tenth percentile, negative-outranks-positive
rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate across valid positions in ten loader batches. 
Larger margins and lower failure rates indicate stronger sampled training 
separation.
- **Training-prefix HR@10:** exact eligible-catalog target hits, averaged within
users then across users; measures in-sample fit.
- **Intervention effects:** changed-minus-clean rank, HR@10, score, sampled 
margin, and top-10 overlap. Positive rank changes indicate deterioration; 
sensitivity itself is not inherently good or bad.

# Perturbation & Tests

Matched recent/older replacements vary dose and 
frequency-random/local-transition-plausible substitutions, preserving occupancy 
and terminal items. Only successful four-plan blocks contribute. Fixed and 
shared restricted catalogs separate candidate insertion effects; inserted-item 
gains are also recorded. Full and terminal-preserving permutations test order 
sensitivity.

Controls check chunked ranking, identical inputs, future-token causality, 
all-padding features, and applicable structurally unreachable positions.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
protocol, coverage, failures, architecture, controls, aggregates, strata, raw 
observations, and cost. Aggregates include exploratory user-bootstrap intervals 
and separate corruption Monte Carlo errors.

Missing evidence remains null or empty. Matching does not equalize embedding 
displacement or exact path counts. Reviews, item categories, simulator traits, 
causal intent, and held-out intervention effects are unavailable. 
Single-category diagnosis supplies no four-category macro estimate; pinned host 
validation HR@10 governs selection. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds 
measured results and definitions into a constrained JSON interpretation request.

