coverage can be expected even under correct uniform sampling. For m draws with 
replacement from M eligible negatives, each competitor has inclusion probability
1−(1−1/M)^m. The audit needs sampler-specific expected coverage, repeated draws,
and uncertainty before interpreting low coverage as a training weakness.', 
'Fresh negatives sampled after training measure current sampler coverage, not 
which competitors the optimizer encountered during training. These claims must 
remain separate unless actual training exposure was logged.', 'The motivating 
margin and catalog-HR measurements use different training examples and 
aggregation schemes. Measure both on identical prefix–target pairs before 
attributing their discrepancy to negative sampling.', 'Captured softmax mass 
includes the target in its denominator, so changes can reflect target confidence
as well as negative coverage. Report target probability and negative-conditional
captured mass separately. Temperature 1 fixes the calculation but does not make 
scores calibrated or comparable across category models.', 'Paired coverage 
differences become undefined when either variant has no strict outrankers. 
Specify complete-pair aggregation, report zero-outranker transitions separately,
and quantify selection caused by failed replacement matching.', 'Reproduction 
still requires concrete negative draw counts, sampling exclusions, replacement 
repetitions, bootstrap counts, scoring precision, runtime caps, and a 
