Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The adapter targets NextItNet: item embeddings feed causal dilated convolutions,
residual blocks and positionwise normalization. Structure inspection also 
recognizes a cumulative-prefix/depth gate that can extend endpoint reach across 
the retained history. Model forward code is not supplied, so structural 
conclusions remain conditional.

`log2feats(sequence)` supplies B × L × D features. Final user representations 
use the **largest nonpadding index**, correctly handling left padding.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the trained network through 
`view.model`, embeddings through `view.item_emb`, mapped histories through 
`view.user_train`, and scores through `view.predict_score(features, items)`.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` consumes up to ten `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` batches and separately samples identified training users. 
Probes run without gradients in evaluation mode; module modes and global random 
states are restored afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Training separation:** positive-minus-negative margin summaries, 
negative-win rate, margin-below-0.5 rate and tie-adjusted pairwise accuracy. 
Better separation suggests stronger sampled training discrimination; margins 
depend on score scale.
- **Representation geometry:** item and endpoint norms, centered covariance 
eigenvalues, leading variance share, entropy effective rank and average angular 
alignment. Concentration can reveal restricted representations, but broader 
geometry does not establish ranking quality.
- **Candidate-depth audit:** training-prefix targets face nested sets of 
99/499/999 negatives over ten repetitions. Reports rank, hit@10, tenth-negative 
margin, eligibility and strata. Up to 50 users receive exact eligible-pool ranks
and hypergeometric sampling expectations; coverage and recommendation frequency 
are descriptive.

# Perturbation & Tests
Identity, batch reordering, future-token changes, reachable-offset checks and 
removable-padding tests examine determinism, causality and padding behavior.

Old/recent deletions measure endpoint training-margin changes. Identified-user 
probes additionally apply random/interior deletion, zero replacement, 
frequency-matched replacement and repeated shuffling at 25%/50% strengths. Fixed
candidate scores measure sensitivity, with paired user bootstrap intervals and 
common-eligibility comparisons. Sensitivity alone does not imply relevance or 
improvement.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including structure, 
checks, representations, training separation, interventions, sensitivity, 
candidate-depth audits, missingness and elapsed time. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests JSON interpretation with status, 
findings, implications and evidence.

Held-out validation interventions and four-category macro results are 
unavailable here. Metadata categories and simulator traits are unobserved. 
Training-prefix targets may have been optimized during fitting; bootstrap 
intervals exclude training-seed and adaptive-search uncertainty. No auxiliary 
predictor is fitted.

