Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The adapter diagnoses one category’s NextItNet model through `ModelView`; the 
full model implementation is not supplied. Structural inspection recognizes 
residual blocks with paired dilated causal convolutions, positionwise LayerNorm,
depth norms, and optional prefix-mean gating. `log2feats(sequence)` returns 
positionwise features. Final sequence representations use the **largest 
nonpadding index**, correctly handling left-padded histories.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
item embeddings through `view.item_emb`, and mapped training histories through 
`view.user_train`. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
tensors shaped B × L. `predict_score(features, items)` scores training pairs and
fixed candidate lists. Probes run without gradients in evaluation mode; module 
modes and global random states are restored afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Training separation:** Up to ten batches provide positive-minus-negative 
margin summaries, negative-win rate, small-margin rate, and tie-adjusted 
pairwise accuracy. Greater separation generally indicates better sampled 
training discrimination; margins depend on score scale.
- **Representation geometry:** Item embeddings and endpoint features yield norm 
summaries, centered covariance spectra, effective rank, leading variance share, 
and mean angular alignment. Low variance or concentrated spectra can flag 
degeneracy, but geometric spread does not establish useful ranking.
- **Candidate-depth audit:** Up to 200 training users have their final training 
interaction ranked from its preceding prefix against nested sets of 99/499/999 
unseen negatives over ten repetitions. Outputs include rank, hit@10, 
tenth-negative margins, strata, and paired uncertainty. Up to 50 users receive 
exact eligible-pool scoring and hypergeometric sampling calibration.

# Perturbation & Tests

Checks cover repeatability, batch reordering, future-token causality, recognized
receptive-field boundaries, and leading-padding removal. Temporal probes delete,
zero, replace with frequency-matched items, or shuffle history regions at 
25%/50% strengths. They measure fixed-pair margin changes and fixed-candidate 
score sensitivity, with eligibility counts and paired user bootstrap intervals. 
Identity changes should be negligible; other changes indicate sensitivity, not 
relevance improvement.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
structural checks, geometry, training separation, sensitivity records, depth 
audits, missingness, and elapsed time. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests a
grounded JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

These are exploratory, category-specific training diagnostics. They establish 
neither held-out validation performance nor four-category macro HR@10. 
Unavailable metadata and simulator traits remain unmeasured; uncertainty 
excludes retraining and adaptive-search variation.

