evaluation users. Sensitivity denominators must distinguish active evaluation 
cases from inactive or equivalent cases without selecting cases using the 
detector itself.', 'With at most 32 users per category before partitioning, 
uncertainty may be substantial. User bootstraps cannot measure variation across 
fault implementations and can give misleadingly narrow intervals when all 
outcomes coincide.', 'Exact mutations, partition sizes, tolerances, fault 
severities, export interfaces and runtime limits remain unspecified. The 
difficulty rating of 5 may underestimate integration work; potential 7 is 
