Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The adapter targets `NextItNetModel`: residual blocks containing two causal 
dilated convolutions. It derives structural dependency offsets from convolution 
kernels and dilations. `log2feats(sequence)` supplies positionwise 
representations shaped **B × L × H**; candidate scores use the **maximum nonzero
position**, correctly handling left padding. The backbone implementation itself 
is not supplied.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual trained module through 
`view.model`, alongside `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, and public 
`user_train` histories. Loader batches contain `(None, sequence, positive, 
negative)` tensors shaped B × L.

`run_full_diagnosis` disables gradients, enters evaluation mode, and restores 
module modes and Python, NumPy, and Torch RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings, excluding 
padding/reserved tokens. Reports `(mean pairwise cosine + 1)/2`; values near 1 
indicate strong alignment, while approximately 0.5 means near-zero average 
cosine. This does not establish diversity or rank collapse.
- **Training margins:** Over ten batches, computes positive-minus-negative 
logits at finite, nonpadding positions. Reports mean, tenth percentile, fraction
below zero, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer ranking reversals 
generally indicate stronger sampled training separation; magnitudes depend on 
score scale.
- **Contract controls:** Checks left-padded readout, batch consistency, 
future-input invariance, dependency boundaries, normalization coupling, and 
synthetic boundary reachability. Export parity compares actual predictor 
scores/ranks when matching checkpoint weights are available.

# Perturbation & Tests

Up to 32 deterministically selected users contribute two training prefixes each,
scored against a target plus 99 unique negatives. Tests compare matched 
older/recent interior deletions, endpoint-preserving reorderings, and 
candidate-disjoint endpoint/interior replacements.

Paired changes measure target rank, target-minus-best-negative margin, and 
HR@10. Lower rank changes and higher margin/hit changes are favorable. Results 
average within users, then across users, with 10,000 user-bootstrap replicates 
and repeated/novel-target strata. Contract failures block sensitivity summaries.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
coverage, exclusions, controls, export status, sensitivity summaries, and a 
trial-local replay manifest. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests a grounded 
JSON interpretation.

These are in-sample diagnostics, not validation improvements. Missing 
measurements remain unavailable; four-category macro results are unset. Reviews,
ratings, item categories, simulator traits, timestamp/text coherence, and 
training-seed/candidate uncertainty are not assessed.

