Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis accesses the NextItNet backbone through a family-specific `ModelView`.
Structural inspection checks residual blocks, dilated temporal convolutions, 
normalization, masking and causal padding. When recognized, the prefix-mean gate
extends potential dependence across the retained history. Backbone 
implementation is not supplied here, so structural conclusions remain 
conditional.

`log2feats(sequence)` returns per-position features. Final sequence 
representations use the **largest nonpadding index**, correctly handling left 
padding. `item_emb` supplies item vectors; `predict_score(features, items)` 
supplies scores.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
mapped training histories through `view.user_train`, and optional metadata. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` reads up to ten `(None, sequence, positive, 
negative)` batches of shape B × L. Probes run without gradients in evaluation 
mode; module modes and global random states are restored afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Training separation:** Positive-minus-negative margins, tenth percentile, 
error rate, margins below 0.5 and tie-adjusted pairwise accuracy. Larger 
positive separation indicates better sampled training discrimination; margins 
depend on score scale.
- **Representation geometry:** Item and endpoint norms, covariance spectra, 
effective rank and angular alignment describe concentration or degeneracy. They 
do not establish ranking quality.
- **User score sensitivity:** Up to 200 training users receive 99 fixed unseen 
training-observed candidates. Absolute and signed score changes measure 
dependence on history, without a universal desirable direction.
- **Candidate-depth audit:** Training-prefix targets face nested 99/499/999 
negatives across ten repetitions. Outputs include ranks, HR@10, tenth-negative 
margins, strata and paired uncertainty. Up to 50 users receive exact 
eligible-pool ranks and hypergeometric sampling expectations; restricted-pool 
coverage and frequency are also reported.

# Perturbation & Tests

Checks cover repeatability, batch reordering, future-token causality, reachable 
offsets and leading-padding removal. Temporal interventions delete, zero, 
frequency-match replace or shuffle history regions at 25%/50% strengths. 
Geometry controls help distinguish content sensitivity from position changes. 
Loader endpoint deletions additionally measure fixed-pair margin changes.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw return contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
eligibility, exclusions, paired records, bootstrap intervals and elapsed time. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests a separate JSON interpretation 
containing status, findings, implications and evidence.

These are exploratory, category-specific training diagnostics—not held-out 
validation results. Missing observations remain unavailable. Bootstrap intervals
exclude training-seed and adaptive-search uncertainty. Ratings, review text, 
categories and simulator traits are unobserved; four-category macro conclusions 
require all four reports.

