Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probe requires the actual trained `NextItNetModel` at `view.model`. It 
inspects item embeddings and intermediate `NextItNetBlock` outputs. 
`view.log2feats(sequence)` supplies finite FP32 representations shaped B × L × 
H; backbone computation is delegated to that adapter. Scoring gathers the final 
nonpadding position using the maximum occupied index, correctly handling left 
padding.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses `item_emb`, `user_train`, `log2feats`, 
and `predict_score`. The loader provides `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
with aligned B × L tensors. Encoded histories and targets are matched against 
training endpoints; ambiguous matches are rejected. Up to 32 users contribute 
one event each, with a target and up to 99 unique unseen alternatives.

Forward hooks capture or replace the final occupied position at two strictly 
intermediate residual blocks. Diagnosis temporarily enables evaluation mode and 
deterministic FP32 execution, then restores modes, backend settings, RNG states,
and hooks.

# Probes & Metrics
Every measured outcome is ``. Larger margins, lower ranks, and higher hit rates 
indicate stronger target ranking. Sensitivity itself is neither inherently good 
nor bad.

Summaries average draws within users, then weight users equally, reporting 
all/repeat/novel strata. Conditional 95% user-bootstrap intervals require at 
least ten users. Endpoint-minus-ordering comparisons use common users. 
Matched-donor summaries report descriptive means, quantiles, and reuse without 
confidence intervals.

Embedding-collapse and loader-wide positive/negative-margin helpers exist but 
are **not invoked** by `run_full_diagnosis`.

# Perturbation & Tests
Stage 1 permutes earlier occupied items or replaces the endpoint, with three 
draws each. Stage 2 runs only when candidate scores change beyond numerical 
tolerance: clean activations restore corrupted recipients, and corrupted 
activations disrupt clean recipients. Additional donors match original history 
length and endpoint.

Controls check readout agreement, batch consistency, bounded future invariance, 
repeatability, hook layout/padding, and no-op/identity patches. Failed sites 
invalidate their patch results.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include
status, summaries, comparisons, donor summaries, controls, coverage, errors, 
numerical configuration, timing, and replay-manifest location.

Measurements concern training-history sensitivity, not host validation or 
generalization. Export parity and complete dependency paths remain unverified. 
Missing metadata, sparse donors, numerical gating, hybrid activations, and the 
120-second category budget limit interpretation; unavailable measurements never 
establish health.

