Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['Mutation routing is 
unspecified: existing probes may call the original ModelView directly and bypass
diagnostic variants. Every tested feature, readout, and scoring path needs 
explicit routing, with reachability witnesses kept separate from detection 
assertions.', 'The future-access mutation changes an earlier feature, but 
ordinary diagnostic outcomes use the final occupied position. A dedicated 
earlier-position causality test must observe the mutation while holding the 
prefix and padding fixed.', 'Constant features can expose history independence, 
but low sensitivity is not a labeled implementation fault in the unmodified 
checkpoint. Unchanged and identity-hook executions establish consistency; they 
do not establish that the original model is fault-free or provide general 
false-positive estimates.', 'Detection rules, mutation strengths, fixed 
constant-feature construction, expected fault-by-probe outcomes, and rate 
denominators are missing. Sixteen users sharing one mutation are correlated test
cases, not sixteen independent faulty implementations; conditional detection 
rates also need coverage and uncertainty.', 'Calibration risks shortcut 
detection if faults are obvious or thresholds are tuned on the same examples. 
Predeclared alarms and separate calibration and assessment cases are needed. The
claimed difficulty of 4 appears optimistic given routing, independent witnesses,
execution-state restoration, and budget enforcement.', 'The proposal does not 
calibrate activation-patch localization itself or verify exported-predictor 
parity. It also lacks a demonstrated path to improved host macro validation 
HR@10. The 20-second allocation needs operation limits and synchronized GPU 
timing; restoration time must remain available.'], generating follow-up queries
