Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The adapter targets NextItNet: causal dilated convolutional residual blocks with
positionwise normalization and explicit padding masks. Structure inspection also
recognizes an optional cumulative-prefix depth gate. The model implementation is
not supplied, so architecture claims depend on inspection and empirical checks.

`view.log2feats(sequence)` produces B × L × D features. Final sequence 
representations use the **largest nonpadding index**, correctly handling 
left-padded histories. `view.predict_score(features, items)` supplies item 
scores; `view.item_emb.weight` supplies item vectors.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
mapped training histories through `view.user_train`, and optional metadata 
through the view. `run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` reads up to ten `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)` batches. It evaluates without gradients and 
restores module modes and Python, NumPy, Torch and CUDA RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Training separation:** Positive-minus-negative margins, tenth percentile, 
negative-win rate, margins below 0.5 and tie-adjusted pairwise accuracy. 
Stronger separation is favorable on sampled training pairs; margins depend on 
score scale.
- **Representation geometry:** Item and endpoint norms, covariance spectra, 
leading variance share and entropy effective rank, before and after 
normalization. Concentration flags limited variation without establishing 
ranking quality. Angular alignment near 0.5 means approximately zero mean 
cosine.
- **Candidate-depth audit:** Up to 200 users’ final training interactions become
targets. Ten nested samples of 99/499/999 unseen negatives measure rank, HR@10 
and tenth-negative margins. Up to 50 users receive exact eligible-pool ranks and
hypergeometric sampling calibration. Coverage and recommendation frequency 
describe restricted-pool outputs.

# Perturbation & Tests
Checks cover repeatability, batch ordering, future-token causality, reachable 
convolution offsets and removal of leading padding. Endpoint probes delete old 
or recent tokens and measure fixed-pair margin changes.

Identified-user probes delete, zero, frequency-match-replace or shuffle history 
regions at 25%/50% strengths. Fixed 99-item candidates isolate absolute and 
signed score changes. Geometry controls, eligibility counts and paired bootstrap
intervals support cautious interpretation; sensitivity alone has no universally 
good direction.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including structure, 
checks, representation statistics, training separation, interventions, 
sensitivity and candidate-depth records, exclusions, strata, uncertainty and 
runtime.

These are exploratory training-data diagnostics. They cannot establish held-out 
performance, causality, intent or simulator traits. Missing evidence is 
explicitly unavailable. Four-category macro results require external 
aggregation. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests an evidence-grounded JSON 
interpretation with status, findings, implications and headline metrics.

