Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied file probes item embeddings and sequence-conditioned scores; it 
does not include the NextItNet implementation. `log2feats(sequence)` produces 
per-position sequence features, and `predict_score(features, items)` scores 
positive and negative targets. The backbone and final user readout cannot be 
verified here. For left-padded histories, the final readout must use the last 
nonpadding position; this probe instead evaluates all valid training positions.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives the compatibility view, stored as 
`self.model`. It accesses `view.item_emb`, `view.model.itemnum`, `log2feats`, 
and `predict_score`. It also retains `meta_data`, `review_data`, and 
`user_train`, although these are unused by the active probes.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped `B 
× L`. Margin analysis uses at most ten batches, switches to evaluation mode, and
disables gradients. Positions contribute only when sequence, positive, and 
negative IDs are all nonzero.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real item embeddings with seed 42,
excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes embeddings, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result through `(mean_cosine + 
1)/2`. Higher values indicate stronger directional alignment; approximately 0.5 
corresponds to zero average cosine. This is a collapse proxy, not measured 
recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes positive minus negative logits at 
valid positions. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins indicate stronger 
separation. Lower `neg_beats_pos_rate` and `small_margin_rate` are preferable; 
their thresholds are margin `< 0` and `< 0.5`, respectively.
- **Breakdown counts:** Reports valid, low-margin, and wrong-rank position 
counts. Item-category breakdowns are explicitly unavailable.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequences are shuffled, masked, reordered, or otherwise perturbed. Random 
embedding subsampling estimates alignment; supplied negatives test 
training-position score separation. Neither tests sequence sensitivity or causal
dependence on history.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing the 
collapse score, four margin summaries, and a nested breakdown. Empty valid 
samples produce placeholder zeros, identifiable through `valid_positions`.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both sections and requests JSON with 
`status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does not 
itself generate that interpretation.

The diagnosis does not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal 
sensitivity, gradients, or simulator traits. Training margins depend on the 
supplied negative samples and logit scale.

